# Every variable below is read by code. If you add one here, add its reader in
# the same change — a settable variable that changes nothing costs the next
# person an afternoon. See corpus/wiki/configuration.md.

# API server port (default 3001). Also the origin the compiled slides name for
# /uploads/* and /assets/fonts/* — both of which the renderer serves from disk
# rather than fetching. See UPLOADS_BASE_URL below.
PORT=3001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accounts, and "Sign in with Ward"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Newspapper has its own accounts: users and sessions live in its SQLite file
# (the `auth_*` tables). Create the first one with the seed script, from a
# shell, never from a file in the repo:
#
#   SEED_USERNAME=... SEED_PASSWORD=... npm run seed --workspace=api
#
# "Sign in with Ward" is a second way in, and optional. With WARD_OIDC_ISSUER
# unset the app runs on local accounts alone and shows no Ward button. With it
# set, the other three are required and the server refuses to boot without them.
# Nothing contacts Ward at boot: a Ward that is down never stops the app from
# starting or a local user from signing in.
#
# Locally, Ward's container (../wzd_auth/infrastructure/local) seeds all five
# into .env and registers this app as a client. In production the deploy
# provides them, and Ward's console registers the client.

# Ward's issuer, as the browser reaches it, ending in /oidc. Plain http: is
# accepted only on loopback.
WARD_OIDC_ISSUER=https://example.com/ward-api/oidc

# This app's slug at Ward.
WARD_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=newspapper

# This app's Ed25519 private key: base64url of a JSON JWK. A SECRET. Never log
# it, never commit it. `npm run oidc-client-key` in Ward prints a fresh pair.
WARD_OIDC_CLIENT_KEY=

# The Ward callback as the BROWSER reaches it. It is this API's own route, under
# the app's base, and must match the client's registration at Ward exactly:
# <origin><base>/api/auth/ward/callback.
WARD_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=https://example.com/newspapper/api/auth/ward/callback

# Optional. Where Ward sends the browser after "sign out of Ward too". Must be
# registered at Ward too.
WARD_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=https://example.com/newspapper/

# Optional. The app's own origin, no path. It decides whether the session cookie
# is `Secure` and what a browser's Origin header must be on sign-in POSTs.
# Defaults to the origin of WARD_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI, then http://localhost:4321.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://example.com

# Optional overrides
# THEME=warm-industrial-1
# NEWSPAPPER_DB_PATH=./data/newspapper.db

# Where uploaded images live. An absolute path puts the store outside the repo;
# a relative one resolves against the repo root, never the cwd. Defaults to
# <repo>/uploads.
UPLOADS_DIR=

# Where rendered runs (output/YYYY-MM-DD-N/) are written, read by
# core/src/util/paths.ts `outputRoot()` and nowhere else. Same rules as
# UPLOADS_DIR. Defaults to <repo>/output. (Not NEWSPAPPER_OUTPUT_DIR: that name
# is the compose file's HOST path for the output mount.)
OUTPUT_DIR=

# Origin the render browser resolves /uploads/<ref> against. Defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:$PORT.
#
# Note that since the Ward cutover the render browser does not actually FETCH
# this: `core/src/render/uploads-route.ts` intercepts the request inside the
# browser context and serves the bytes from disk, which is what let /uploads/*
# become a guarded route. The URL still has to be well-formed — it is what the
# compiled slide's CSS `url()` contains — but nothing listens on it during a
# render.
UPLOADS_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Reader (stored feed items, refreshed in the background)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Minutes between background refreshes of every enabled feed; 0 turns the loop off.
READER_REFRESH_MINUTES=30

# Days a fetched item is kept; each source always keeps its newest 50 regardless.
READER_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# The path the UI is served under. A build arg in the deploy; in `npm run dev`
# the UI dev server reads it from here, so local dev is laid out like the deploy.
# Open http://localhost:4321/newspapper/.
#
# The API reads it too, at RUNTIME, for one thing: the session cookie's Path.
# That must be the base, so the browser also sends the cookie with the <img>
# requests for /output/* and /uploads/*, which sit beside /api, not under it.
# In the deploy it must therefore be in the container's environment, not only
# the build arg. Unset, it is read back from WARD_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI.
NEWSPAPPER_BASE=/newspapper/
